{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "A dataset's metadata document, schema version 1.0",
  "description": "The assembly of version 1.0's field rows into the document one dataset's metadata is judged against. Each field's value is referenced out of its row under fields/ rather than copied, so the row stays the one place the field is defined. The record that carries a field's absence state is written here once and applies to every field, as docs/decisions/absence.md fixes its shape. What this schema cannot refuse is listed in deferred_checks, and what nothing refuses at all is listed in not_refused_anywhere; the two are separate because a judgement filed among the validator's checks would read as a refusal somebody is going to write.",
